{
  "name": "aphid",
  "_about": "The pea aphid (Acyrthosiphon pisum), 4 mm long: a soft green pear, broad behind; a small head with red eyes and antennae longer than the body swept back over it; two long tubes (siphunculi) sticking up and back from the rear and a short tail between them; long thin legs with dark knees and feet; a beak folded under it for sucking sap. Variant: the winged form, two pairs of clear wings held roof-wise past the tail. Coats: the black bean aphid (Aphis fabae), a pink pea aphid. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
